# motor_control.options - nanopb field size constraints for motor_control.proto
# These settings optimize for ESP32 embedded use with static allocation.
#
# STAR Project - Texas A&M University

# Emergency stop reason (max_size:128)
# Rationale: 128 bytes accommodates typical emergency stop reason strings
# (e.g., "USER_REQUESTED", "COLLISION_DETECTED", "LOW_BATTERY", etc.)
# Typical short reason codes (~10-20 bytes) leave ample room within the
# 128-byte buffer for future verbose diagnostics if needed.
# Frame overhead + protobuf encoding leaves sufficient room in the MTU.
# If comprehensive stack traces or detailed diagnostics are needed, consider
# increasing to 256 bytes or using a repeated string field.
star.v1.EmergencyStopRequest.reason     max_size:128
